# Question 6: Find All Unique Items Purchased

**Problem Statement:**

A customer purchases several items, including repeated items. Write a Java program using a `LinkedHashSet` to display only unique items in the order they were purchased.

**Sample Input:**

```text
7
Laptop
Mouse
Keyboard
Mouse
Headphones
Laptop
Monitor
```

**Sample Output:**

```text
Unique Items Purchased:
Laptop
Mouse
Keyboard
Headphones
Monitor
```

**Java Code:**

```java
import java.util.LinkedHashSet;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        LinkedHashSet<String> items = new LinkedHashSet<>();

        int n = sc.nextInt();
        sc.nextLine();

        // Add purchased items
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            String item = sc.nextLine();
            items.add(item);
        }

        // Display unique items in purchase order
        System.out.println("Unique Items Purchased:");

        for (String item : items) {
            System.out.println(item);
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}
```

**Concept Used:**

* **LinkedHashSet:** Stores only unique elements and maintains insertion order.
* **add():** Adds an item if it is not already present.
* **Duplicate Removal:** Repeated items are automatically ignored.
* **Insertion Order:** Items appear in the order they were first purchased.
